  <h2>This week</h2>
  <p>Finishing the empirical section of the NMTC paper. I'm rerunning the CDE-FE decomposition with a slightly different rural definition (a continuous rurality index from ERS rather than the binary metro/non-metro flag). The headline result is robust so far, but the within-CDE coefficient picks up a small amount of significance with the continuous specification, which I want to understand before I let the paper near a referee.</p>

  <p>Katia's first wave of Portugal interview emails went out yesterday. Five replies back so far, which is a higher hit rate than I expected. AD&C said yes to a 45-minute meeting and offered to share aggregated PT 2030 disbursement data subject to a research-use agreement, which would be a coup. Banco de Portugal Economics Research deferred until July, polite but firm.</p>

  <p>The hub you're reading this on is also getting iteratively better. I keep noticing things that should be different and changing them. The reading aggregator is up to seven feeds healthy out of twelve.</p>

  <h2>This month</h2>
  <p>The NMTC paper needs to be on SSRN before I start traveling. NEUDC submission deadline is late July. Three chapter drafts for <em>Pictures of Inference</em> are queued up: the conditional-quantile picture, the network-econometrics picture, and the shock-propagation picture. I'd like to ship at least one of them.</p>

  <p>Liz is going to be in town for ten days starting next week. We're going to use part of that time to push the EffDist documentation toward a Zenodo release. We've been calling that done for three months and it isn't.</p>

  <h2>What I'm not doing</h2>
  <p>I keep getting asked about LLM-and-economics takes. I don't have a coherent one and I'm not going to manufacture one for engagement.</p>

  <p>I'm not taking institutional consulting engagements until the NMTC paper is on SSRN. There's a Maryland-state evaluation that's been sitting in my inbox for two months. I will get to it.</p>

  <p>I am not on Twitter. The handle is dormant. I check Bluesky once a day, mostly to read what the development-econ people are flagging.</p>

